      "status": "Answered",
      "question": "How should one autonomous Stage-B run sequence the fleet rollout?",
      "answer": "Use the three Public Canaries first, followed by deterministic profile waves with lexicographically ordered repositories and a hard completion gate between waves.",
      "evidence": "The user selected Canary + Wellen (Recommended)."
    },
    {
      "id": "IAD002",
      "status": "Answered",
      "question": "Which completion boundary must the later Stage-B run satisfy?",
      "answer": "MergeAndSync: Stage B completes only after required target pull requests are merged, default branches are synchronized, and full fleet convergence is proven. Fresh execution authority remains mandatory.",
      "evidence": "The user selected MergeAndSync (Recommended) as the future delivery boundary."
    },
    {
      "id": "IAD003",
      "status": "Answered",
      "question": "How should a rollout-wave failure be handled?",
      "answer": "Stop fail-closed, preserve already merged targets, and resume the same run only after full fleet and authority revalidation; do not continue best effort or auto-revert successful merges.",
      "evidence": "The user selected Stop und Resume (Recommended)."
    }
